  "status_text": "Checked in Lean from the desk in the last half hour: to represent the 7-by-7 crown takes at least 22 AND/OR gates of fan-in at most two, one more than three a side, so a floor of 3n is not the whole truth there. Also checked: any AND/OR circuit representing the crown on n a side gives one of no more gates for \"at least two of n inputs are on\". From above we hold circuits of 3n plus a square-root term (computed), so, if the conjectured floor of 3n is right at every size, the hunt for this one graph is down to that term.",
